<title>THAILAND: Italian-Thai, Degremont to build water plant.</title>
<headline>Italian-Thai, Degremont to build water plant.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major Thai constructor Italian-Thai Development Plc said on Friday it has joined with France's Degremont S.A. and a Thai firm to build a water plant for the Thai government.</p>
<p>The company said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand that the plant, worth 870.87 million baht ($33.49 million), is to be built for the state-run Metropolitan Waterworks Authority.</p>
<p>Construction work would take two years, it said.</p>
<p>Italian-Thai was trading at 133 baht, down two baht, at 0745 GMT on Friday. (US$1=26 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
